  {
   "id": 676853,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Jamal’s company is looking to expand into a market in West Africa, but Jamal wants to ensure that there are roads, bridges, nearby airports, and shipping terminals from which to distribute the product. Jamal is examining the country’s ________.",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1344664,
     "content_html": "infrastructure",
     "correctness": "1.0",
     "feedback_html": "Infrastructure is the basic physical systems of a nation, such as roads, sewage treatment, communication, water treatment, etc."
    },
    {
     "id": 1344663,
     "content_html": "governmental stability",
     "correctness": "0.0",
     "feedback_html": "That&#8217;s not correct. Governmental stability would assess how receptive it is to foreign firms and the complexity of the governmental bureaucracy."
    },
    {
     "id": 1344662,
     "content_html": "inflation and unemployment rates",
     "correctness": "0.0",
     "feedback_html": "That&#8217;s not correct. Inflation and unemployment rates are important to assess when marketing internationally, but these are economic factors."
    },
    {
     "id": 1344661,
     "content_html": "culture",
     "correctness": "0.0",
     "feedback_html": "That&#8217;s not correct. Culture is important to assess when marketing internationally, but Jamal is not examining cultural factors."
    }
   ],
